--- begin ---
PRE-REGISTRATION: layer overlap (--overlap-layers), YOLOv8s, warm dispatch A/B. Desktop 2 (DESKTOP-CBL5NUA),
2026-10-15. Written before any timed dispatch of the overlap container. Its only device runs so far: the exactness
check (results/aie/overlap_layers_exact_yolov8s_desktop2_20261015T2057Z: 300 dispatches each, 0 differ, heads equal
to yolov8s_ab_ctl's). No timing from that run is read.

Change. The emitter drops the barrier after each layer. Each fill or drain instead waits for exactly the
earlier-layer tasks it conflicts with in the workspace (RAW, WAR, WAW at exact 8-byte cells,
compiler/layer_overlap.py); a frame barrier ends the stream. Proved hazard-free offline over the emitted stream for
YOLOv8s and YOLOv8n with an independent exact-byte checker that does find hazards when the waits are withheld
(tests/test_layer_overlap_offline.py). The default build is byte-identical to the shipped stream.

Containers: build/yolov8s_ab_ctl.ignite (control) and build/yolov8s_ol_ov.ignite (same build + --overlap-layers;
same instruction-stream size, 933,028 B, reordered awaits). Hashes below.

Method: tools/bench_dispatch_ab.py --pair overlap=build/yolov8s_ab_ctl.ignite,build/yolov8s_ol_ov.ignite --rounds 4
--iters 300 (real and all-NOP copies, one process per run, order reversed every second round), under
research-lowlevel.sh --npu; void unless timing_eligible true.

What it can recover (DERIVED, from the tail sitting 20261015T1959Z): the gap at each boundary, not the cores' busy
backlog. Over the 65 boundaries: NOP tail 1,385,276 + next lead 124,108 + one quad's transit 441,119 =
1,950,503 cycles = 1.084 ms at 1.80 GHz; the NOP tail alone 0.770 ms. The offline predictor finds the next layer's
first fill pushable before the previous layer is known complete at all 65 boundaries.

Prediction: real delta (test - control) between -0.30 and -1.10 ms; NOP delta between -0.30 and -1.10 ms, and NOP
gains at least as much as real less 0.2 ms (the NOP frame has the same boundaries and no compute to hide behind).

Rules (on the 4-round means):
- KILL: real delta > -0.10 ms, or the test lower in fewer than 3 of 4 rounds.
- PASS: real delta <= -0.30 ms with the test lower in 4 of 4 rounds.
- else MARGINAL.
Reported, not verdict-bearing: NOP delta; compute exposure change (real - NOP).
Named alternatives for any gain: dispatch-to-dispatch drift (controlled by interleaving and 4 rounds); a different
instruction count (none: same stream size, same task count per layer, offline-checked). For a loss: hazard-free
waits that serialize more than the barrier did (the stream awaits specific tasks earlier), which would show as a
NOP loss too.

A hang, an exactness failure or contention voids the sitting.
--- end ---

